LLM Output #0:
 Description: This Terraform configuration creates an ElastiCache user group named `elasticache-user-group` and adds three users to it. The users are `user1`, `user2`, and `user3`.

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

locals {
  elasticache_user_group_name = "elasticache-user-group"
  elasticache_users = ["user1", "user2", "user3"]
}

resource "aws_elasticache_user_group" "elasticache_user_group" {
  group_name = local.elasticache_user_group_name
}

resource "aws_elasticache_user" "elasticache_users" {
  for_each = { for user in local.elasticache_users : user => user }
  user_name = each.value

  group_name = aws_elasticache_user_group.elasticache_user_group.group_name
}
```

This configuration uses the `aws` provider with the `us-west-2` region. It defines a local variable `elasticache_user_group_name` for the ElastiCache user group name, and another local variable `elasticache_users` for the list of users. The `aws_elasticache_user_group` resource creates the ElastiCache user group, and the `aws_elasticache_user` resource adds each user to the group. The `for_each` loop is used to create one `aws_elasticache_user` resource for each user in the `elasticache_users` list.

