 **Description:**

This Terraform configuration will create an Amazon S3 bucket to store images for a website. The bucket will be secure and accessible only to the specified IAM user. The configuration includes an IAM role for the S3 bucket to allow it to make calls to other AWS services on behalf of the specified IAM user.

**Terraform HCL:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

locals {
  bucket_name = "my-website-images-${random_id.id.hex}"
}

resource "random_id" "id" {
  byte_length = 4
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "s3_access" {
  name = "s3_access_for_website_images"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "s3.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_policy" "s3_bucket_policy" {
  name = "s3_bucket_policy_for_website_images"
  path = "/"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "s3:PutObject",
          "s3:GetObject",
          "s3:ListBucket"
        ]
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Resource = "${aws_s3_bucket.images.arn}/*"

        Principal = {
          AWS = "${aws_iam_user.website_user.arn}"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_user_to_role_mapping" "s3_user_to_role" {
  user = aws_iam_user.website_user.name
  role = aws_iam_role.s3_access.name
}

resource "aws_iam_user" "website_user" {
  name = "website_user"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "images" {
  bucket = local.bucket_name
  acl    = "private"
}
```

**Explanation:**

- The `provider` block sets the AWS provider and region.
- `local` and `random_id` resources are used to generate a unique bucket name.
- An IAM role (`aws_iam_role.s3_access`) is created for the S3 bucket to allow it to make calls to other AWS services on behalf of the specified IAM user.
- An IAM policy (`aws_iam_policy.s3_bucket_policy`) is created to grant the specified IAM user (`aws_iam_user.website_user`) permissions to put, get, and list objects in the S3 bucket.
- The IAM user is mapped to the IAM role (`aws_iam_user_to_role_mapping.s3_user_to_role`).
- An IAM user (`aws_iam_user.website_user`) is created for the specified user who will manage the images.
- An S3 bucket (`aws_s3_bucket.images`) is created with a private ACL.

This configuration is deployable with Terraform ~> 1.9.8 and hashicorp/aws ~> 5.75.

